
- ESP32
- WiFi support
- 202 APA102 RGB LEDs arranged in a ring
- 4 WS2812 RGB LEDs
- 4 capacitence touch sesoors (wires from pins to expost metal)
- the WS2812 LEDs are each associated with one capacitance sensor
- the WS2812 LEDs are located evenely spaced just outside the ring
  - the expeact positioning of those relative to the ring start will have to be configurable
- the WS2812 LEDs assume the same color as the average of the 5 or so closest pixels to them, a wheighted average favoring the closest would be good
- the touch sensors cause the cooresponding WS2812 LED to flash
- the touch sensors by default cause an entry into a local mode, 255 for cycle through local modes
- the ring pixels are exposed as one strip, the WS2812 LEDs need not be exposed.
- the touch sensors are to be exposed
- local modes include
  - the usual ones
  - modes that use the ring, making a seamless effect not exposing the start and end of the ring
- if the sink protocol cannot be implemnted in the ESP32 then a simpler protocol may be used between the the ESP32 and a sink protocol program on a Linux host
